; A dedicated parse-time performance regression test (asm/docs/corpus.md's
; floats.c "One shared timeout" follow-up). See test_parse_perf.ml.
;
; An executable plus a rule rather than a (test) stanza, the same shape
; test/props uses and for the same reason: (test) would put its executable in
; this directory's @all alias regardless of enabled_if, which matters once
; ASM_MELANGE=true disables driver.
;
; Native only: this needs Unix for wall-clock timing, the one thing js_of_ocaml
; and Melange builds have no reason to exercise identically (a browser/Node
; run's own timing is not the claim this test makes) - and driver itself is
; gated the same way, so this follows its own dependency's own gate.

(executable
 (name test_parse_perf)
 (modes exe)
 (libraries driver unix)
 (enabled_if
  (<> %{env:ASM_MELANGE=false} true)))

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (action
  (run ./test_parse_perf.exe))
 (enabled_if
  (<> %{env:ASM_MELANGE=false} true)))
